  "question": {
    "text": "For a particular reversible reaction at temperature $T, \\Delta H$ and $\\Delta S$ were found to be both $+v e$. If $T_e$ is the temperature at equilibrium, the reaction would be spontaneous when",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lGBKs",
      "text": "\n$T_e>T$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Gg4QF",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{T}>\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{e}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "qGwO3",
      "text": "\n$T_e$ is 5 times $T$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nZttx",
      "text": "\n$T =T_e$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\Delta \\mathrm{G}=\\Delta \\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{T} \\Delta \\mathrm{S}\n$$\nat equilibrium, $\\Delta \\mathrm{G}=0$\nfor a reaction to be spontaneous $\\Delta$ G should be negative\n$$\n\\therefore \\mathrm{T}>\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{e}}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
